{"chapters": [{"id": "to-be", "title_de": "Das Verb „to be“ (am/is/are)", "explanation_de": "„to be“ hat im Präsens drei Formen: I am, he/she/it is, you/we/they are. Kurzformen: I'm, he's, she's, it's, you're, we're, they're. Verneinung mit „not“: I'm not, he isn't, they aren't (NICHT „I amn't“). Fragen bilden Sie durch Umstellung: Are you tired? Is she at home? Kurze Antworten: Yes, I am. / No, she isn't. – Achtung: In Kurzantworten mit „Yes“ keine Kurzform („Yes, I am“, nicht „Yes, I'm“). Typischer Fehler deutscher Lerner: Alter mit „have“ – richtig ist „I am 30 (years old)“, nicht „I have 30 years“.", "examples": [{"en": "I am a teacher.", "de": "Ich bin Lehrer/in."}, {"en": "She isn't at home.", "de": "Sie ist nicht zu Hause."}, {"en": "Are they from Berlin?", "de": "Sind sie aus Berlin?"}, {"en": "My son is ten years old.", "de": "Mein Sohn ist zehn Jahre alt."}], "exercises": [{"type": "gap", "prompt": "___ (be) your parents at home?", "answer": "Are", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Frage: Verb nach vorn; parents = they"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "She ___ a doctor.", "options": ["is", "are", "am", "be"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "she → is."}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "I am from Austria. (Verneinung)", "answer": "I'm not from Austria.", "accepted": ["I am not from Austria."], "hint_de": "am + not"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "My sister ___ (be) 25 years old.", "answer": "is", "accepted": ["'s"], "hint_de": "Eine Person (she) → is"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "My keys ___ on the table.", "options": ["is", "are", "am", "be"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "keys = Plural → are."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "How old ___ you?", "options": ["have", "is", "are", "do"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "Alter mit „to be“; you → are."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "This ___ my friend Anna.", "options": ["be", "are", "am", "is"], "answer": 3, "why_de": "this → is."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "___ he your brother?", "options": ["Is", "Am", "Are", "Does"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "Frage mit he → Is he ...?"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "I ___ (be not) hungry.", "answer": "am not", "accepted": ["'m not"], "hint_de": "„I amn't“ gibt es nicht"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "You are late. (Frage)", "answer": "Are you late?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Umstellung"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "They are in the garden. (Frage)", "answer": "Are they in the garden?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Verb vor das Subjekt"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "It ___ (be) cold today.", "answer": "is", "accepted": ["'s"], "hint_de": "it → is"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "The children ___ (be not) at school today.", "answer": "aren't", "accepted": ["are not"], "hint_de": "Plural + Verneinung"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Tom and I ___ (be) good friends.", "answer": "are", "accepted": ["'re"], "hint_de": "Tom and I = we → are"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "Are you tired? – Yes, I ___.", "options": ["'m", "am", "are", "is"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "In Kurzantworten mit Yes keine Kurzform."}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "She is a student. (Verneinung)", "answer": "She isn't a student.", "accepted": ["She's not a student.", "She is not a student."], "hint_de": "is + not"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "It is expensive. (Verneinung)", "answer": "It isn't expensive.", "accepted": ["It's not expensive.", "It is not expensive."], "hint_de": "is + not"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "I ___ 40 years old.", "options": ["has", "is", "am", "have"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "Alter: to be, nicht have."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "We ___ (be) from Hamburg.", "answer": "are", "accepted": ["'re"], "hint_de": "we → are"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "I ___ (be) a nurse.", "answer": "am", "accepted": ["'m"], "hint_de": "I → am"}], "level": "A1"}, {"id": "present-simple", "title_de": "Present Simple", "explanation_de": "Das Present Simple verwenden Sie für Gewohnheiten, Routinen und allgemeine Tatsachen. In der 3. Person Singular (he/she/it) hängt man -s an: she works, he goes (-es nach o, s, sh, ch, x), she studies (Konsonant + y → -ies). Verneinung und Frage mit do/does: I don't like, she doesn't like, Do you like? Does he like? Nach does steht das Verb OHNE -s (Does she work? – nicht „Does she works?“). Signalwörter: always, usually, often, sometimes, never, every day, on Mondays. Typischer Fehler: „He go“ (fehlendes -s) oder Fragen ohne do („Like you coffee?“).", "examples": [{"en": "She works in an office.", "de": "Sie arbeitet in einem Büro."}, {"en": "I don't eat meat.", "de": "Ich esse kein Fleisch."}, {"en": "Does he play football?", "de": "Spielt er Fußball?"}, {"en": "Water boils at 100 degrees.", "de": "Wasser kocht bei 100 Grad."}], "exercises": [{"type": "transform", "prompt": "My parents live in Bonn. (Verneinung)", "answer": "My parents don't live in Bonn.", "accepted": ["My parents do not live in Bonn."], "hint_de": "parents = they → don't"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "He works at the weekend. (Frage)", "answer": "Does he work at the weekend?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Does + Subjekt + Grundform"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "My boss never ___ late.", "options": ["arrives", "arrive", "is arrive", "arriving"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "my boss = he/she → -s."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "The shop ___ (open) at 9 o'clock.", "answer": "opens", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "the shop = it → -s"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "You like pizza. (Frage)", "answer": "Do you like pizza?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Do + Subjekt + Grundform"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "She ___ (work) in a bank.", "answer": "works", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "3. Person Singular: -s"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "He ___ (study) English at university.", "answer": "studies", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Konsonant + y → -ies"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "They ___ to the gym on Mondays.", "options": ["going", "go", "are go", "goes"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "they → Grundform."}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "She speaks Spanish. (Verneinung)", "answer": "She doesn't speak Spanish.", "accepted": ["She does not speak Spanish."], "hint_de": "doesn't + Grundform ohne -s"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "He ___ coffee every day.", "options": ["drinking", "is drink", "drinks", "drink"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "3. Person Singular: drinks."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "My cat ___ (go) outside every morning.", "answer": "goes", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "nach -o: -es"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "___ you speak French?", "options": ["Is", "Are", "Does", "Do"], "answer": 3, "why_de": "Frage mit you → Do."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "My father ___ (watch) the news every evening.", "answer": "watches", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "nach -ch: -es"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "We ___ (not / like) horror films.", "answer": "don't like", "accepted": ["do not like"], "hint_de": "we → don't + Grundform"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "___ (do) your brother live in London?", "answer": "Does", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "brother = he → Does"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "What time ___ the train leave?", "options": ["does", "has", "do", "is"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "the train = it → does."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "She doesn't ___ fish.", "options": ["liking", "like", "to like", "likes"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "Nach doesn't steht die Grundform."}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "I play tennis. (Verneinung)", "answer": "I don't play tennis.", "accepted": ["I do not play tennis."], "hint_de": "don't + Grundform"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "Does your sister ___ in Munich?", "options": ["lives", "living", "live", "is live"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "Nach does: Grundform ohne -s."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Anna ___ (not / drive) to work.", "answer": "doesn't drive", "accepted": ["does not drive"], "hint_de": "she → doesn't + Grundform"}], "level": "A1"}, {"id": "present-continuous", "title_de": "Present Continuous", "explanation_de": "Das Present Continuous (am/is/are + Verb-ing) beschreibt, was gerade jetzt oder vorübergehend passiert: I'm reading. She's working from home this week. Signalwörter: now, right now, at the moment, today, this week, Look!, Listen! Schreibregeln: stummes -e fällt weg (make → making), kurzer betonter Vokal + Konsonant → Verdopplung (sit → sitting, run → running), -ie → -ying (lie → lying). Zustandsverben wie like, know, want, need, understand stehen normalerweise NICHT in der -ing-Form: I know (nicht „I'm knowing“). Typischer Fehler deutscher Lerner: Das Deutsche hat keine Verlaufsform, daher wird oft „I read now“ statt „I'm reading now“ gesagt.", "examples": [{"en": "I'm reading a book at the moment.", "de": "Ich lese gerade ein Buch."}, {"en": "Look! It's raining.", "de": "Schau! Es regnet."}, {"en": "They aren't working today.", "de": "Sie arbeiten heute nicht."}, {"en": "What are you doing?", "de": "Was machst du gerade?"}], "exercises": [{"type": "gap", "prompt": "We ___ (not / watch) TV now.", "answer": "aren't watching", "accepted": ["are not watching", "'re not watching"], "hint_de": "are + not + -ing"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "I am working. (Verneinung)", "answer": "I'm not working.", "accepted": ["I am not working."], "hint_de": "am + not"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "He is wearing a jacket. (Frage)", "answer": "Is he wearing a jacket?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Is vor das Subjekt"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "I ___ what you mean.", "options": ["understand", "am understand", "am understanding", "understanding"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "understand ist ein Zustandsverb, keine -ing-Form."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Why ___ (be) he crying?", "answer": "is", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Fragewort + is + he + -ing"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "What ___ you doing?", "options": ["does", "are", "is", "do"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "Present Continuous: are + you + -ing."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "I ___ (write) an email right now.", "answer": "am writing", "accepted": ["'m writing"], "hint_de": "stummes -e fällt weg"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "You are reading. (Frage mit „What“)", "answer": "What are you reading?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "What + are + you + -ing"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "She ___ a new car. She doesn't like her old one.", "options": ["wanting", "is wanting", "wants", "want"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "want ist ein Zustandsverb."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Listen! Somebody ___ (sing).", "answer": "is singing", "accepted": ["'s singing"], "hint_de": "somebody → is"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "Sorry, I can't talk. I ___.", "options": ["'m drive", "drive", "drives", "'m driving"], "answer": 3, "why_de": "Gerade jetzt → am driving."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Look! The baby ___ (sleep).", "answer": "is sleeping", "accepted": ["'s sleeping"], "hint_de": "is + -ing"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "Be quiet! The children ___.", "options": ["are sleeping", "is sleeping", "sleep", "sleeps"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "Jetzt gerade, Plural → are sleeping."}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "They are playing football. (Frage)", "answer": "Are they playing football?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Are vor das Subjekt"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "They ___ (sit) in the garden at the moment.", "answer": "are sitting", "accepted": ["'re sitting"], "hint_de": "Konsonant verdoppeln: sitting"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "He ___ a shower at the moment.", "options": ["is have", "is having", "have", "has"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "„have a shower“ ist eine Handlung → -ing möglich."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "___ (be) you listening to me?", "answer": "Are", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Frage: Are you ...?"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "Look! It ___.", "options": ["snow", "snowing", "is snowing", "snows"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "Look! → gerade jetzt."}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "She is cooking. (Verneinung)", "answer": "She isn't cooking.", "accepted": ["She's not cooking.", "She is not cooking."], "hint_de": "is + not"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "She ___ (run) in the park right now.", "answer": "is running", "accepted": ["'s running"], "hint_de": "run → running"}], "level": "A1"}, {"id": "there-is-are", "title_de": "There is / There are", "explanation_de": "Mit „there is / there are“ sagen Sie, dass etwas irgendwo existiert (deutsch: „es gibt“, „da ist“). Singular und nicht zählbare Nomen: There is (there's) a bank. There is some milk. Plural: There are two cafés. Verneinung: There isn't a ..., There aren't any ... Frage: Is there a ...? Are there any ...? Kurzantwort: Yes, there is. / No, there aren't. Typischer Fehler deutscher Lerner: „It gives a supermarket“ – das ist falsch, richtig ist „There is a supermarket“.", "examples": [{"en": "There is a supermarket near my flat.", "de": "Es gibt einen Supermarkt in der Nähe meiner Wohnung."}, {"en": "There are three bedrooms.", "de": "Es gibt drei Schlafzimmer."}, {"en": "Is there a bus stop here?", "de": "Gibt es hier eine Bushaltestelle?"}, {"en": "There isn't any milk in the fridge.", "de": "Es ist keine Milch im Kühlschrank."}], "exercises": [{"type": "choice", "prompt": "There isn't ___ bread left.", "options": ["any", "many", "some", "a"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "Verneinung + nicht zählbar → any."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "How many people ___ there in your family?", "answer": "are", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "How many + Plural → are"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "There ___ two banks in the town centre.", "options": ["be", "are", "is", "has"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "Plural → are."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "How many rooms ___ in the flat?", "options": ["has it", "is there", "are there", "there are"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "Frage: How many + are there."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "There ___ (be) a park near my house.", "answer": "is", "accepted": ["'s"], "hint_de": "Singular → is"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "There are some apples. (Frage)", "answer": "Are there any apples?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Frage: some → any"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "There is a garden. (Verneinung)", "answer": "There isn't a garden.", "accepted": ["There's no garden.", "There is not a garden."], "hint_de": "is + not"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "There ___ (be) twenty students in the class.", "answer": "are", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Plural → are"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "___ there a chemist's near here?", "answer": "Is", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Singular-Frage: Is there"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "There ___ (not / be) any chairs in the room.", "answer": "aren't", "accepted": ["are not"], "hint_de": "Plural verneint"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "There is a cinema in the town. (Frage)", "answer": "Is there a cinema in the town?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Is there ...?"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "There ___ (be) some cheese in the fridge.", "answer": "is", "accepted": ["'s"], "hint_de": "cheese ist nicht zählbar → is"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "There is one bathroom. (Plural: two)", "answer": "There are two bathrooms.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Plural → are + -s"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Is there a lift? – Yes, there ___.", "answer": "is", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Kurzantwort ohne Kurzform"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "There are some pens on the desk. (Verneinung)", "answer": "There aren't any pens on the desk.", "accepted": ["There are no pens on the desk.", "There are not any pens on the desk."], "hint_de": "some → any"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Are there any eggs? – No, there ___.", "answer": "aren't", "accepted": ["are not"], "hint_de": "Kurzantwort Plural verneint"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "___ any shops in your village?", "options": ["Have there", "Is there", "There are", "Are there"], "answer": 3, "why_de": "Frage, Plural → Are there."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "There ___ a lot of traffic today.", "options": ["is", "have", "are", "be"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "traffic ist nicht zählbar → is."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "___ a good restaurant in this street.", "options": ["There are", "There's", "It's", "It gives"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "„Es gibt“ = there is."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "Is there a hotel near the station? – Yes, ___.", "options": ["it is", "there's", "there is", "is there"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "Kurzantwort mit Yes: keine Kurzform."}], "level": "A1"}, {"id": "articles-nouns", "title_de": "Artikel, Plural, zählbar/nicht zählbar", "explanation_de": "„a“ steht vor Konsonantenlauten (a book, a university), „an“ vor Vokallauten (an apple, an hour) – entscheidend ist der Laut, nicht der Buchstabe. „the“ verwendet man, wenn klar ist, welches Ding gemeint ist, oder bei Einzigartigem (the sun). Berufe brauchen „a/an“: She is a doctor (deutsch: „Sie ist Ärztin“ ohne Artikel!). Allgemeine Aussagen im Plural oder mit nicht zählbaren Nomen ohne Artikel: I like dogs. Life is short. Plural: meist -s, nach s/sh/ch/x -es (boxes), Konsonant + y → -ies (cities); unregelmäßig: man → men, woman → women, child → children, person → people, foot → feet, tooth → teeth. Nicht zählbar (kein a/an, kein Plural): water, money, information, advice, furniture, news, bread.", "examples": [{"en": "She is an engineer.", "de": "Sie ist Ingenieurin."}, {"en": "The children are in the garden.", "de": "Die Kinder sind im Garten."}, {"en": "Can you give me some information?", "de": "Können Sie mir einige Informationen geben?"}, {"en": "I love cats.", "de": "Ich liebe Katzen."}], "exercises": [{"type": "transform", "prompt": "This is a box. (Plural: These ...)", "answer": "These are boxes.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "is → are, box → boxes"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "Can you close ___ door, please?", "options": ["the", "–", "a", "an"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "Es ist klar, welche Tür gemeint ist."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "I don't like ___ coffee.", "options": ["a", "–", "the", "an"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "Allgemeine Aussage, nicht zählbar: kein Artikel."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "I waited for ___ hour.", "answer": "an", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "„hour“ beginnt mit Vokallaut (h stumm)"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "I have a tooth problem. (Ersetze „a tooth problem“ durch „two bad teeth“)", "answer": "I have two bad teeth.", "accepted": ["I've got two bad teeth.", "I have got two bad teeth.", "I've two bad teeth."], "hint_de": "tooth → teeth"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "I need an information. (Korrigiere den Fehler)", "answer": "I need some information.", "accepted": ["I need information."], "hint_de": "information ist nicht zählbar"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Two ___ (child) are playing outside.", "answer": "children", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "unregelmäßiger Plural"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "She studies at ___ university in Leeds.", "answer": "a", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "„university“ beginnt mit /j/-Laut → a"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "I need new ___ (shoe).", "answer": "shoes", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "regelmäßiger Plural"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "There are four ___ in the car.", "options": ["peoples", "person", "people", "persons people"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "Plural von person: people."}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "He is engineer. (Korrigiere den Fehler)", "answer": "He is an engineer.", "accepted": ["He's an engineer."], "hint_de": "Beruf → a/an; Vokallaut → an"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "My brother is ___ architect.", "answer": "an", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Vokallaut → an"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "___ moon is very bright tonight.", "options": ["An", "A", "–", "The"], "answer": 3, "why_de": "Einzigartig → the."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Five ___ (woman) work in this office.", "answer": "women", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "unregelmäßiger Plural"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "London and Paris are big ___ (city).", "answer": "cities", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Konsonant + y → -ies"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "My mother is ___ nurse.", "options": ["a", "an", "the", "–"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "Berufe brauchen a/an."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "There are three ___ (box) in the car.", "answer": "boxes", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "nach x: -es"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "The man is tall. (Plural)", "answer": "The men are tall.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "man → men"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "How much ___ do you need?", "options": ["monies", "money", "a money", "moneys"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "money ist nicht zählbar."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "She gave me some good ___.", "options": ["advices", "a advice", "advice", "an advice"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "advice ist nicht zählbar."}], "level": "A1"}, {"id": "possessives-pronouns", "title_de": "Possessivbegleiter, Objektpronomen, Genitiv-'s", "explanation_de": "Subjektpronomen: I, you, he, she, it, we, they. Objektpronomen (nach Verben und Präpositionen): me, you, him, her, it, us, them – „Call me“, „with them“. Possessivbegleiter (vor einem Nomen): my, your, his, her, its, our, their. Possessivpronomen (allein stehend): mine, yours, his, hers, ours, theirs. Achtung: „its“ (sein/ihr, besitzanzeigend) hat KEINEN Apostroph; „it's“ = it is. Ebenso „their“ (ihr) ≠ „they're“ (they are) ≠ „there“ (dort). Besitz bei Personen mit 's: Tom's car, my parents' house (Plural auf -s: nur Apostroph), the children's toys. Typischer Fehler: „his“ für eine Frau verwenden – im Englischen richtet sich his/her nach dem Besitzer, nicht nach dem Ding.", "examples": [{"en": "This is my sister's car.", "de": "Das ist das Auto meiner Schwester."}, {"en": "Can you help me?", "de": "Kannst du mir helfen?"}, {"en": "Their house is bigger than ours.", "de": "Ihr Haus ist größer als unseres."}, {"en": "The dog wants its food.", "de": "Der Hund will sein Futter."}], "exercises": [{"type": "gap", "prompt": "Peter and Sue live with ___ children. (= ihre Kinder)", "answer": "their", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Besitzer Plural → their"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "We're lost. Can you help ___?", "answer": "us", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Objektpronomen von we"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "Please give ___ the book.", "options": ["me", "I", "mine", "my"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "Nach dem Verb: Objektpronomen."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "I don't know those people. Do you know ___?", "options": ["theirs", "them", "their", "they"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "Objektpronomen von they."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "Where are ___ keys? I can't find them.", "options": ["me", "I", "my", "mine"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "Vor einem Nomen: Possessivbegleiter my."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "The cat is drinking ___ milk.", "answer": "its", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "its ohne Apostroph"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "___ the children's toys.", "options": ["Those is", "This is", "These is", "These are"], "answer": 3, "why_de": "toys = Plural → these are."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Is this your pen? – No, it isn't ___. (= meiner)", "answer": "mine", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Possessivpronomen allein stehend"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "This book belongs to me. (It's ...)", "answer": "It's mine.", "accepted": ["It is mine."], "hint_de": "Possessivpronomen"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "This is the car of my brother. (Mit Genitiv-'s)", "answer": "This is my brother's car.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Besitzer + 's + Ding"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "These are the bikes of the children. (Mit Genitiv-'s)", "answer": "These are the children's bikes.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "children's"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "I see she every day. (Korrigiere den Fehler)", "answer": "I see her every day.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Objektpronomen: her"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "I like Mark. I often play tennis with ___.", "answer": "him", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Objektpronomen von he"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "The dog is in it's basket. (Korrigiere den Fehler)", "answer": "The dog is in its basket.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "its ohne Apostroph"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Anna loves ___ job. (= Annas Job)", "answer": "her", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Besitzerin ist eine Frau → her"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "That's ___ (Tom) bike.", "answer": "Tom's", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Genitiv-'s"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "This is my ___ (parents) house.", "answer": "parents'", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Plural auf -s: nur Apostroph"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "My ___ name is Laura.", "options": ["wife's", "wives", "wifes", "wife"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "Genitiv: wife's."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "John is washing ___ car.", "options": ["him", "his", "her", "its"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "Besitzer ist John → his."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "This bag isn't hers. It's ___.", "options": ["us", "our's", "ours", "our"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "Allein stehend: ours."}], "level": "A1"}, {"id": "can", "title_de": "Can / can't (Fähigkeit, Erlaubnis, Bitte)", "explanation_de": "„can“ drückt Fähigkeit (I can swim), Möglichkeit, Erlaubnis (You can sit here) und höfliche Bitten (Can you help me?) aus. „can“ ist für alle Personen gleich – kein -s: she can (nicht „she cans“). Danach folgt die Grundform OHNE „to“: I can speak (nicht „I can to speak“). Verneinung: can't / cannot (in einem Wort geschrieben). Frage: Can you ...? Kurzantwort: Yes, I can. / No, I can't. Typischer Fehler deutscher Lerner: Fragen mit „do“ bilden („Do you can ...?“) – das ist falsch.", "examples": [{"en": "I can play the guitar.", "de": "Ich kann Gitarre spielen."}, {"en": "She can't drive.", "de": "Sie kann nicht Auto fahren."}, {"en": "Can I open the window?", "de": "Darf ich das Fenster öffnen?"}, {"en": "Can you speak more slowly, please?", "de": "Können Sie bitte langsamer sprechen?"}], "exercises": [{"type": "gap", "prompt": "Where ___ I park my car?", "answer": "can", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Fragewort + can + Subjekt"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "Can I use your phone? – Yes, of course you ___.", "options": ["can", "may to", "are", "do"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "Kurzantwort mit can."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Sorry, we ___ (can / not) come to your party.", "answer": "can't", "accepted": ["cannot"], "hint_de": "Verneinung"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "Do you can help me? (Korrigiere den Fehler)", "answer": "Can you help me?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Frage ohne do"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "I ___ (can / not) find my glasses.", "answer": "can't", "accepted": ["cannot"], "hint_de": "Verneinung"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "You can drive. (Frage)", "answer": "Can you drive?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Can vor das Subjekt"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "My son ___ (can) swim very well.", "answer": "can", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "can hat nie ein -s"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Can you ski? – No, I ___.", "answer": "can't", "accepted": ["cannot"], "hint_de": "Kurzantwort verneint"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "___ you help me with this bag?", "answer": "Can", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Frage: Can + Subjekt"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "He can't ___ because he's ill.", "options": ["comes", "come", "coming", "to come"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "Grundform nach can't."}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "I can to speak English. (Korrigiere den Fehler)", "answer": "I can speak English.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "kein to nach can"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "She can ___ (speak) three languages.", "answer": "speak", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Nach can: Grundform ohne to"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "She cans dance. (Korrigiere den Fehler)", "answer": "She can dance.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "kein -s bei can"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "He can cook. (Verneinung)", "answer": "He can't cook.", "accepted": ["He cannot cook."], "hint_de": "can + not"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "___ you swim?", "options": ["Are", "Does", "Can", "Do"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "Frage mit can, kein do."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "I can ___ you tomorrow.", "options": ["calling", "calls", "to call", "call"], "answer": 3, "why_de": "Grundform nach can."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Can they come tomorrow? – Yes, they ___.", "answer": "can", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Kurzantwort bejaht"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "She ___ play the piano.", "options": ["can", "can to", "is can", "cans"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "can: immer gleich, ohne to."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "My grandmother ___ use a computer.", "options": ["don't can", "can't", "not can", "doesn't can"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "Verneinung: can't."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "___ I ask you a question?", "options": ["Does", "Do", "Can", "Am"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "Erlaubnis: Can I ...?"}], "level": "A1"}, {"id": "prepositions", "title_de": "Präpositionen der Zeit und des Ortes (in/on/at)", "explanation_de": "Zeit: „at“ für Uhrzeiten und feste Ausdrücke (at 7 o'clock, at night, at the weekend – britisch), „on“ für Tage und Daten (on Monday, on 3 May, on my birthday), „in“ für Monate, Jahre, Jahreszeiten und Tagesteile (in July, in 2020, in summer, in the morning). Ohne Präposition: today, tomorrow, yesterday, next week, last year, every day. Ort: „in“ = in einem Raum/Gebiet (in the kitchen, in London), „on“ = auf einer Fläche (on the table, on the wall), „at“ = an einem Punkt oder Ort einer Tätigkeit (at the bus stop, at work, at home, at school). Typischer Fehler deutscher Lerner: „in the weekend“ oder „on the morning“ – richtig: at the weekend, in the morning.", "examples": [{"en": "The meeting is at 10 o'clock on Monday.", "de": "Das Meeting ist am Montag um 10 Uhr."}, {"en": "I was born in 1985.", "de": "Ich bin 1985 geboren."}, {"en": "The picture is on the wall.", "de": "Das Bild hängt an der Wand."}, {"en": "She's at work.", "de": "Sie ist bei der Arbeit."}], "exercises": [{"type": "transform", "prompt": "We met in Friday. (Korrigiere den Fehler)", "answer": "We met on Friday.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Wochentag → on"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "I was born ___ 12 March.", "options": ["on", "–", "in", "at"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "Datum → on."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "It's cold ___ winter.", "options": ["on", "in", "at", "–"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "Jahreszeit → in."}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "See you on next week. (Korrigiere den Fehler)", "answer": "See you next week.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "next week ohne Präposition"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "She works on a bank. (Korrigiere den Fehler)", "answer": "She works in a bank.", "accepted": ["She works at a bank."], "hint_de": "in a bank"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "I usually read ___ the evening.", "answer": "in", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Tagesteil → in the evening"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "The milk is ___ the fridge.", "options": ["on", "to", "in", "at"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "im Inneren → in."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Your keys are ___ the table.", "answer": "on", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Fläche → on"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "I can't sleep ___ night.", "options": ["by", "in", "on", "at"], "answer": 3, "why_de": "feste Wendung: at night."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "I'm sorry, Mr Smith isn't here. He's ___ home.", "answer": "at", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "feste Wendung: at home"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "She lives ___ Manchester.", "answer": "in", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Stadt → in"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "I go swimming at the morning. (Korrigiere den Fehler)", "answer": "I go swimming in the morning.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "in the morning"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "The children are ___ school.", "options": ["at", "by", "to", "on"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "at school = in der Schule (Tätigkeit)."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "My birthday is ___ June.", "answer": "in", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Monat → in"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "See you ___ tomorrow!", "options": ["on", "–", "in", "at"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "tomorrow ohne Präposition."}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "I get up on 7 o'clock. (Korrigiere den Fehler)", "answer": "I get up at 7 o'clock.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Uhrzeit → at"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "We have English ___ Tuesdays.", "answer": "on", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Wochentag → on"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "The film starts ___ 8 pm.", "answer": "at", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Uhrzeit → at"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "There's a spider ___ the ceiling!", "options": ["in", "at", "on", "by"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "Fläche → on."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "We often go cycling ___ the weekend.", "answer": "at", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "britisch: at the weekend"}], "level": "A1"}, {"id": "questions", "title_de": "Fragewörter und Wortstellung in Fragen", "explanation_de": "Fragewörter: what (was), where (wo/wohin), when (wann), who (wer), why (warum), how (wie), which (welche/r), whose (wessen), how much (wie viel – nicht zählbar), how many (wie viele – zählbar), how old, how often, what time. Wortstellung: Fragewort + Hilfsverb (do/does/is/are/can/did) + Subjekt + Verb: Where do you live? What is she doing? When can you come? Fragt man nach dem Subjekt selbst, entfällt do/does: Who lives here? (nicht „Who does live here?“). Typischer Fehler deutscher Lerner: Verb direkt nach vorn stellen wie im Deutschen („Where live you?“) – im Englischen braucht man do/does.", "examples": [{"en": "Where do you live?", "de": "Wo wohnst du?"}, {"en": "What time does the bus leave?", "de": "Wann fährt der Bus ab?"}, {"en": "How many brothers have you got?", "de": "Wie viele Brüder hast du?"}, {"en": "Who lives next door?", "de": "Wer wohnt nebenan?"}], "exercises": [{"type": "choice", "prompt": "Who ___ in this flat?", "options": ["lives", "does live", "do live", "live"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "Frage nach dem Subjekt: ohne does."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "___ much does this jacket cost?", "answer": "How", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Preis → How much"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "Where you live? (Korrigiere den Fehler)", "answer": "Where do you live?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Hilfsverb do fehlt"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "He is reading a magazine. (Frage mit „What“)", "answer": "What is he reading?", "accepted": ["What's he reading?"], "hint_de": "What + is + he + -ing"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "What ___ you do at the weekend?", "options": ["are", "do", "does", "is"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "you → do."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "___ are you sad? – Because I lost my phone.", "answer": "Why", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Grund → Why"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "Where ___ ?", "options": ["you work", "you do work", "do you work", "work you"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "Fragewort + do + Subjekt + Verb."}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "She lives in Leeds. (Frage nach dem Ort mit „Where“)", "answer": "Where does she live?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Where + does + she + live"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "___ is your birthday? – In May.", "answer": "When", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Zeitpunkt → When"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Where ___ your sister work?", "answer": "does", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "sister = she → does"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "___ often do you go to the cinema?", "options": ["Which", "What", "When", "How"], "answer": 3, "why_de": "Häufigkeit → How often."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "___ do you live? – In Berlin.", "answer": "Where", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Ort → Where"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "___ is that woman? – She's my teacher.", "options": ["Who", "Whose", "What", "Which"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "Person → Who."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "___ colour do you prefer, red or blue?", "options": ["Who", "Which", "Whose", "How"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "Auswahl aus wenigen → Which."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "___ many children have they got?", "answer": "How", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "zählbar → How many"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "___ bag is this? – It's Maria's.", "answer": "Whose", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Besitz → Whose"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "Tom plays the guitar. (Frage nach dem Subjekt mit „Who“)", "answer": "Who plays the guitar?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Subjektfrage ohne does"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "They start work at 8. (Frage mit „What time“)", "answer": "What time do they start work?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "What time + do + they"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "What time ___ the shop close?", "options": ["is", "has", "does", "do"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "the shop = it → does."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "___ old is your daughter? – She's six.", "answer": "How", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Alter → How old"}], "level": "A1"}, {"id": "past-to-be", "title_de": "Vergangenheit von „to be“ (was/were)", "explanation_de": "Die Vergangenheit von „to be“: I/he/she/it was, you/we/they were. Verneinung: wasn't, weren't. Frage durch Umstellung: Were you at home? Was it expensive? Kurzantworten: Yes, I was. / No, they weren't. Signalwörter: yesterday, last night/week/year, ago (two days ago), in 2010. Feste Wendungen: I was born in ... (geboren werden ist immer Vergangenheit: nicht „I am born“). Typischer Fehler deutscher Lerner: „you was“ – richtig ist immer „you were“, auch bei einer Person.", "examples": [{"en": "I was tired yesterday.", "de": "Ich war gestern müde."}, {"en": "We weren't at home last night.", "de": "Wir waren gestern Abend nicht zu Hause."}, {"en": "Were you at the party?", "de": "Warst du auf der Party?"}, {"en": "She was born in 1990.", "de": "Sie wurde 1990 geboren."}], "exercises": [{"type": "gap", "prompt": "Was the film good? – No, it ___.", "answer": "wasn't", "accepted": ["was not"], "hint_de": "Kurzantwort verneint"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "I am tired. (Vergangenheit, „yesterday“ am Ende)", "answer": "I was tired yesterday.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "am → was"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "They were happy. (Frage)", "answer": "Were they happy?", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Were vor das Subjekt"}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "You was right. (Korrigiere den Fehler)", "answer": "You were right.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "you → were"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "It ___ cold two days ago.", "options": ["was", "were", "is", "has"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "ago → Vergangenheit, it → was."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "Where ___ (be) you on Saturday?", "answer": "were", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Fragewort + were + you"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "How ___ your holiday?", "options": ["were", "was", "is been", "did"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "holiday = it → was."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "The weather ___ (be not) very good last week.", "answer": "wasn't", "accepted": ["was not"], "hint_de": "it → wasn't"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "___ (be) you at home last night?", "answer": "Were", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "you → were"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "___ your parents at the wedding?", "options": ["Was", "Did", "Were", "Are they"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "Plural → Were."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "We ___ (be not) late this morning.", "answer": "weren't", "accepted": ["were not"], "hint_de": "we → weren't"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "Was she at the meeting? – Yes, she ___.", "options": ["were", "is", "did", "was"], "answer": 3, "why_de": "Kurzantwort: was."}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "We are in London. (Vergangenheit, „last week“ am Ende)", "answer": "We were in London last week.", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "are → were"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "They ___ (be) in Italy last summer.", "answer": "were", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "they → were"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "The shops ___ open on Sunday.", "options": ["weren't", "wasn't", "didn't", "not were"], "answer": 0, "why_de": "Plural verneint → weren't."}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "I ___ born in 1978.", "options": ["am", "was", "have", "were"], "answer": 1, "why_de": "geboren: was born."}, {"type": "transform", "prompt": "He was at school. (Verneinung)", "answer": "He wasn't at school.", "accepted": ["He was not at school."], "hint_de": "was + not"}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "I ___ (be) at work yesterday.", "answer": "was", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "I → was"}, {"type": "choice", "prompt": "You ___ very quiet yesterday.", "options": ["be", "was", "were", "are"], "answer": 2, "why_de": "you → immer were."}, {"type": "gap", "prompt": "My grandparents ___ (be) born in Poland.", "answer": "were", "accepted": [], "hint_de": "Plural → were"}], "level": "A1"}]}